 "_readme": "YC companies that are NOT in the public Algolia directory index, recovered two ways and carried as first-party site evidence (COLLECTION.md §1: a listing on the investor's own site, ANY era, suffices for membership on its own). `live_page_unindexed`: /companies/<slug> returns 200 and the page's own Inertia payload carries the full company record, but the slug is absent from the ycdc_public-tagged search index — including batch_name 'ycc_only', YC's own marker for a Continuity-only holding that never went through a batch (Monzo). `delisted_archived`: the slug 404s on the live site today and the record comes from the Internet Archive capture of its company page. Both classes were found by paging the archived /companies/ CDX namespace and probing each slug against the live site; a 301 meant a rename or an id-form URL and became an identity merge instead (decisions.md R1, R3). Three slugs in this namespace are YC founder-community pages, not companies (black-founders, hispanic-latino-founders, women-founders); they are filtered here and listed in wayback.non_company_slugs.",
